    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0875" n="1383" xml:id="pg1383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/9–848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-08T15:00:00+03:00">September 8,
                            1948—3 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1261. In speech over Transjordan controlled Ramallah radio on 5th Azmi
                    Nashashibi, director station and brigadier in Arab Legion, indicated Arabs might
                    consider direct talks with Jews under following “conditions”: Jews return to
                    areas held before November 29, return of all Arab refugees, payment by Jews for
                    damages. Jews not attempt to dictate to Arabs. Although conditions mentioned
                    obviously inacceptable, speech significant as further indication possible Arab
                    willingness negotiate directly with Jews.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
